# Push descriptors (28 Nov, DXVK-style): the pixel shader's textures and samplers (set 3) are pushed into the command
# buffer per draw with vkCmdPushDescriptorSetKHR (VK_KHR_push_descriptor, enabled by SDK own patch 0032) instead of
# a set found in this submission's map or allocated and updated (texture sets were ~0.76 ms and updates ~0.20 ms a
# frame at ~7,000 draws in qos_218). Only one set of a layout can be pushed, so vertex textures keep their sets; a
# layout's pixel set is pushed when its textures + samplers fit maxPushDescriptors (at most 32). A push is skipped
# when the last draw pushed the same handles with the same layout, nothing bound since (same_layout) and in the
# same texture_sets_epoch_. Recorded at the binds, after the pass and its transfers. BOTS_GFX_PUSH_DESCRIPTORS=0
# turns it off (A/B). The sub-profile line adds "pixel textures pushed N, push skipped M". Changed layouts mean the
# driver's pipeline cache misses once (pipelines rebuilt at the first start).
  src/gfx/vk/draw.cpp     | 79 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
  src/gfx/vk/renderer.cpp |  4 +--
  src/gfx/vk/renderer.h   | 20 +++++++++++--
  src/gfx/vk/vk_api.h     |  6 ++++
  4 files changed, 101 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

